WEBVTT

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:51.051
Is there any problem?

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.095
No, sir. How was the station?

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:54.596
No problem.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:57.766
Hey, why isn't anyone guarding the platform?

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:03.480
Because it's too dangerous...
when the train comes.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.524
The train?

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:36.430
<i>School never taught me what friends are</i>

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:41.810
<i>People are such difficult creatures</i>

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.231
<i>This world where you never</i>
<i>know what's said behind your back</i>

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:51.778
<i>Looks a little ugly to me</i>

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:56.658
<i>Compassion and ego sway on the scales</i>

00:01:56.658 --> 00:02:01.205
<i>They've swayed ever since I met you</i>

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:04.124
<i>Your trespassing did a number on me</i>

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:08.420
<i>It's not like anyone would do</i>

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:08.504
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:09.671
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:13.926
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:13.926 --> 00:02:18.263
<i>Like a fish out of water</i>

00:02:18.263 --> 00:02:20.557
<i>Delicacy and literacy</i>

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:23.143
<i>Might not be necessary</i>

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:26.313
<i>I just want to be wanted</i>

00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:28.732
<i>Selfish little me</i>

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:32.903
<i>The scales have tipped</i>

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:35.155
<i>As friends</i>

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:41.161
<i>Let's meet in a secret place</i>

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:54.633
That's enough for now. Have the men rest up.

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:58.846
This is a bad idea, Lieutenant!
I don't trust them.

00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:01.390
Master Sergeant, don't make me say it again!

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.269
Yes, sir.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.611
I apologize for my subordinates' rudeness.

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:17.990
I don't know how much more their minds can take.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.868
I hate to have to ask you this,

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:24.872
but could you avoid provoking them?

00:03:24.872 --> 00:03:26.373
Sure.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.002
Understood.

00:03:32.796 --> 00:03:36.049
Sir, Lieutenant Drake reporting.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.634
Come in.

00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:44.224
Who are they?

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:47.686
They're civilians we encountered
on the way back from our ground recon.

00:03:47.686 --> 00:03:49.354
Their entry point?

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:53.066
Unknown. They were already
here before they knew it.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.068
Do you know the general location?

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:59.531
My best guess is the wild things' territory.

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:04.703
The Horned Man, face dogs, and
Walking Gallows were after them.

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:10.125
Send out a scouting party at dawn.
I'll leave the members up to you.

00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:15.422
Understood. But the area is full of bear traps.

00:04:15.422 --> 00:04:20.469
How did you two manage to get through there?

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:24.223
They followed the train tracks.

00:04:24.223 --> 00:04:28.060
We have yet to find
a bear trap along the tracks.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:28.894
But before that--

00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:30.938
We were just lucky!

00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:38.695
Ending up in a place like
this is hardly what I'd call lucky.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:45.160
I'm Major Ray Barker,

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:49.206
the current commander of this unit.

00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:50.916
I'm Toriko Nishina.

00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:53.377
I-I'm Sorawo Kamikoshi.

00:04:53.377 --> 00:04:54.962
You're students?

00:04:54.962 --> 00:04:57.840
U-University students... from Tokyo.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.508
Tokyo...

00:04:59.508 --> 00:05:04.263
It's getting harder and harder to
cling to the notion that we're lost

00:05:04.263 --> 00:05:07.391
in the mountains of Okinawa.

00:05:07.391 --> 00:05:12.145
Um, what did you mean by "current commander"?

00:05:13.981 --> 00:05:18.068
We've suffered many
casualties since we've been here.

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:22.698
And more than a few of my men became
mentally unstable and went missing.

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:30.330
Even worse are those whose minds
or bodies were altered by bear traps.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:34.126
Most of them were put down
by their own comrades.

00:05:34.126 --> 00:05:39.590
However, a few ran off,
but not before causing casualties.

00:05:40.924 --> 00:05:42.759
Are you two all right?

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:46.930
Now's the time to speak up
if you feel something is wrong.

00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:49.308
--We're fine!
--Yeah, fine!

00:05:49.308 --> 00:05:50.392
I see.

00:05:50.392 --> 00:05:52.644
If any female squad members were still alive,

00:05:52.644 --> 00:05:55.105
I'd have them conduct a physical exam.

00:05:55.105 --> 00:05:58.734
But I'll just have to take your word for it.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:02.696
That's very... gentlemanly of you.

00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:06.158
We'd quickly become no more than beasts

00:06:06.158 --> 00:06:09.328
if we didn't try to remain civilized out here.

00:06:09.328 --> 00:06:12.623
If it came to that,
all hope of escape would be lost.

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:15.918
Who knows when we, too,
might descend into savagery?

00:06:15.918 --> 00:06:19.129
Even if we don't, we'll end up starving to death

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:23.008
or being attacked and killed by the wild things.

00:06:23.008 --> 00:06:24.968
What about your armored vehicles?

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.387
We don't have enough diesel fuel.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:30.682
We've had to prioritize it
for our electric generators.

00:06:30.682 --> 00:06:34.645
Even if we had enough fuel,
I wouldn't dare use our vehicles,

00:06:34.645 --> 00:06:39.483
now that we know how the bear traps
can alter mechanical equipment.

00:06:39.483 --> 00:06:42.736
It's like we're surrounded
in a hidden minefield,

00:06:42.736 --> 00:06:47.991
boxing us in within the confines of
the station and its surrounding area.

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:50.953
There aren't any bear traps
on the tracks, right?

00:06:50.953 --> 00:06:52.996
Why not move your men that way?

00:06:52.996 --> 00:06:54.665
Of course, we tried that.

00:06:54.665 --> 00:07:00.504
We sent a squad in each direction,
but only a single soldier returned.

00:07:02.089 --> 00:07:05.300
He came leisurely strolling
back as if taking a walk.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:11.890
And he was humming as he
deliberately carved up his face...

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:15.686
with his trusty old Ka-Bar knife.

00:07:20.274 --> 00:07:22.693
You're welcome to one of the empty tents.

00:07:22.693 --> 00:07:26.572
Tomorrow morning, I'd like you
to accompany our scouts

00:07:26.572 --> 00:07:28.907
to your estimated entry point.

00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:30.033
O-Okay.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.618
Understood.

00:07:32.661 --> 00:07:34.288
Please use this tent.

00:07:34.288 --> 00:07:36.331
Thank you.

00:07:37.499 --> 00:07:39.459
Wait one second.

00:07:40.752 --> 00:07:42.588
We don't have much, but here.

00:07:42.588 --> 00:07:43.380
--Huh?

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.883
--Are you sure?
--Huh?

00:07:45.883 --> 00:07:48.969
I'd like to maintain my humanity.

00:07:48.969 --> 00:07:52.222
Otherwise, when we get back to our world,

00:07:52.222 --> 00:07:56.143
I won't be able to look
my loved ones in the eye.

00:07:57.603 --> 00:07:59.730
Thank you.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:04.985
Also, I'd advise against using your phones.

00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:11.617
This place is a mess.

00:08:11.617 --> 00:08:13.619
Yeah.

00:08:13.619 --> 00:08:15.954
Looks like I can use my phone.

00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:17.331
Huh?

00:08:22.044 --> 00:08:24.796
They must have a cell tower.

00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:28.800
I've got one, no three bars now.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.470
It's not very stable, but it might work.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.181
Hey, let's try.

00:08:34.181 --> 00:08:36.099
Who do you wanna call?

00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:39.102
Hmmm... Kozakura?

00:08:39.102 --> 00:08:45.150
What? I-I don't know her number. You call her!

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:50.197
I would, but my display is all weird.

00:08:50.197 --> 00:08:52.115
Do you know her number?

00:08:52.115 --> 00:08:55.202
Yeah. It's zero-nine-zero...

00:08:59.706 --> 00:09:01.625
It's ringing.

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:02.918
Put it on speaker.

00:09:02.918 --> 00:09:06.505
Okay. But I wonder why he
told us not to use our phones.

00:09:06.505 --> 00:09:09.299
Didn't he just "advise" against it?

00:09:09.299 --> 00:09:11.885
That's true, but...

00:09:13.095 --> 00:09:14.096
Hello?

00:09:14.096 --> 00:09:18.642
Ah! Hello? Kozakura, is that you?

00:09:18.642 --> 00:09:19.810
Who's this?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:22.604
Oh, um, i-it's Kamikoshi.

00:09:22.604 --> 00:09:27.860
Oh, Sorawo? What is it?
Something happen to that other idiot?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:28.986
I'm right here!

00:09:28.986 --> 00:09:30.487
That figures.

00:09:30.487 --> 00:09:33.866
What do you want?
And where are you calling from?

00:09:33.866 --> 00:09:36.493
What's that sound? It's really loud.

00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:39.621
Sorry. I think we have a bad connection.

00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:42.791
Tell whoever's behind you to shut up.

00:09:42.791 --> 00:09:44.334
Huh?

00:09:47.254 --> 00:09:48.172
Well?

00:09:48.172 --> 00:09:49.882
Oh, um...

00:09:49.882 --> 00:09:53.051
We're calling from the Otherside.

00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:57.222
Huh? Your call got through?
You gotta be kidding me!

00:09:57.222 --> 00:10:01.101
Y-Yeah, crazy, right? But it's the truth.

00:10:01.101 --> 00:10:05.063
There are soldiers here. US forces from Japan!

00:10:07.107 --> 00:10:10.652
Hmm... They said Pale Horse Battalion?

00:10:10.652 --> 00:10:13.155
Not Dark Horse Battalion?

00:10:13.155 --> 00:10:15.282
They never mentioned that.

00:10:15.282 --> 00:10:17.159
Why bring it up?

00:10:17.159 --> 00:10:19.411
I'd understand if it were Dark Horse.

00:10:19.411 --> 00:10:22.080
They're a next-gen-equipment-testing unit.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.250
It's no surprise they have
an infantry support robot.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.045
And they really are deployed in Okinawa.

00:10:28.045 --> 00:10:32.591
But I've never come across
the name Pale Horse before.

00:10:32.591 --> 00:10:33.592
So?

00:10:33.592 --> 00:10:36.261
It must be a covert unit.

00:10:36.261 --> 00:10:38.472
They were very clear about the name.

00:10:38.472 --> 00:10:40.557
They could be lying to you.

00:10:40.557 --> 00:10:45.312
If not, then they're not worried
about you leaking their secret.

00:10:45.312 --> 00:10:47.856
Wait. Does that mean they're gonna eliminate us?

00:10:47.856 --> 00:10:53.070
No. There are plenty of
gentler ways to keep people quiet.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.988
Or at least I would hope.

00:10:54.988 --> 00:10:59.660
But from what you've said,
it sounds like they are really on edge.

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:04.164
They'll probably get trigger happy if they
see how your bodies have been altered.

00:11:04.164 --> 00:11:06.041
If you remain there--

00:11:06.041 --> 00:11:07.751
--What are we gonna do?
Even if we fled, where would we go?

00:11:07.751 --> 00:11:10.045
--Listen, Sorawo...
--What are we gonna do?
Even if we fled, where would we go?

00:11:10.045 --> 00:11:14.466
You're not going anywhere! Stay right there!

00:11:14.466 --> 00:11:18.095
Wait... What did she just say?

00:11:18.095 --> 00:11:21.139
You're not going anywhere!

00:11:24.184 --> 00:11:27.855
For your own safety, please stand back.

00:11:27.855 --> 00:11:31.692
Next stop, Kisaragi...

00:11:31.692 --> 00:11:34.319
Kisaragi Station?

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:36.029
Kozakura?

00:11:36.029 --> 00:11:42.494
The train is about to arrive.
Please stand behind the white line.

00:11:42.494 --> 00:11:44.788
Better hurry!

00:11:44.788 --> 00:11:47.374
The platform is the blue light of death.

00:11:47.374 --> 00:11:52.129
Do that while watching the dolphin video.

00:11:52.129 --> 00:11:54.882
It will pass through the crossing shortly.

00:11:54.882 --> 00:11:58.468
A monkey train like those
often found in amusement parks.

00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:04.558
A senior citizen with wire is coming.

00:12:36.882 --> 00:12:38.884
Sorawo.

00:12:38.884 --> 00:12:42.930
Wh-What's the matter with Kozakura?

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:48.018
Toriko, let's worry about ourselves right now.

00:12:48.018 --> 00:12:50.479
Yeah but, why would she--

00:12:50.479 --> 00:12:54.775
The faster we get out of here,
the sooner we can go check on her.

00:12:54.775 --> 00:12:58.362
We're heading back to our world, okay?

00:13:00.072 --> 00:13:02.574
Okay, got it.

00:13:07.788 --> 00:13:11.500
This is why I advised you not to use your phone.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.418
Don't move from this spot.

00:13:13.418 --> 00:13:15.879
The battle is about to begin.

00:14:01.758 --> 00:14:03.719
Music?

00:14:22.946 --> 00:14:24.615
Fire!

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.661
Fire!

00:14:40.422 --> 00:14:42.716
Die, die, die!

00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:46.345
Bastard! Damn bastard!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:01.860
It's like they're trying to scare us.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.362
Huh?

00:15:11.245 --> 00:15:13.080
A cow?

00:15:14.248 --> 00:15:15.499
All right.

00:15:15.499 --> 00:15:16.667
What's that?

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:21.421
Um, it's called an M14 EBR.

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:22.798
Oh...

00:15:22.798 --> 00:15:26.760
Why even ask if you won't understand the answer?

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:29.263
So, what's my target?

00:15:29.263 --> 00:15:32.599
About ten feet above that mass of faces.

00:15:32.599 --> 00:15:34.268
Got it.

00:15:36.854 --> 00:15:38.188
What's so funny?

00:15:38.188 --> 00:15:43.652
I checked the scope... even though
I can't see what I'm shooting.

00:15:43.652 --> 00:15:45.654
Well, give it a try.

00:15:45.654 --> 00:15:48.448
Roger. One shot-in-the-dark coming up!

00:15:50.409 --> 00:15:52.327
A little lower.

00:15:54.997 --> 00:15:57.416
How's that? Did I hit it?

00:15:57.416 --> 00:15:59.543
Doesn't look like it.

00:15:59.543 --> 00:16:01.420
I wonder why.

00:16:02.921 --> 00:16:06.258
Is it because she's shooting
at something she can't see?

00:16:06.258 --> 00:16:10.220
Does perceptual awareness
influence targeting precision?

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.097
Toriko, give me the rifle. I'll give it a try.

00:16:12.097 --> 00:16:15.225
Hey! What do you think you're doing!

00:16:15.225 --> 00:16:17.394
Get down from there, now!

00:16:17.394 --> 00:16:18.437
Hurry.

00:16:18.437 --> 00:16:19.605
You know how to use it?

00:16:19.605 --> 00:16:20.689
Gimme a hand.

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:21.690
Come on!

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.317
Yes, sir!

00:16:24.318 --> 00:16:26.028
Hold me steady.

00:16:29.198 --> 00:16:30.574
Roger.

00:16:57.017 --> 00:16:58.936
What happened?

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:03.315
Yeah!

00:17:03.315 --> 00:17:03.607
--We did it!

00:17:03.607 --> 00:17:05.442
--We did it!
--God damn it!

00:17:05.442 --> 00:17:08.529
--Did you guys do that? Holy cow!

00:17:08.529 --> 00:17:09.863
The creatures are gone!

00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:11.949
Hell yeah! We did it.

00:17:11.949 --> 00:17:15.244
Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:17:15.244 --> 00:17:20.874
Maybe I was wrong about
you two. If so, I apologize.

00:17:20.874 --> 00:17:22.918
Forgive me.

00:17:27.089 --> 00:17:29.925
Your eye...

00:17:31.093 --> 00:17:34.054
Sorawo, your color contact is gone!

00:17:35.097 --> 00:17:36.390
I knew it.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:41.103
You're... one of them.

00:17:41.103 --> 00:17:41.937
Run!

00:17:41.937 --> 00:17:42.771
Stop!

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:44.815
What's going on here? Greg!

00:17:44.815 --> 00:17:46.149
Sir!

00:17:47.276 --> 00:17:49.653
Hey, you two! Wait!

00:17:49.653 --> 00:17:50.863
That way's too dangerous!

00:17:50.863 --> 00:17:53.740
Sir, they are one of them!

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:55.325
Let's go!

00:17:55.325 --> 00:17:57.244
Stop, Greg!

00:18:14.344 --> 00:18:16.597
The railroad crossing.

00:18:16.597 --> 00:18:18.056
It's coming!

00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:21.185
The train! The Meat Train!

00:18:24.521 --> 00:18:27.274
Hurry! We've gotta get across the tracks!

00:18:27.274 --> 00:18:30.235
Wait. I'll check for glitches.

00:18:33.697 --> 00:18:35.115
That's it!

00:18:35.115 --> 00:18:37.576
Toriko, that's our ticket out of here!

00:18:38.577 --> 00:18:38.952
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"

00:18:38.952 --> 00:18:40.329
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
The train?

00:18:40.329 --> 00:18:43.207
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
I can see our world and the
Otherside superimposed over it.

00:18:43.916 --> 00:18:47.002
I bet it'll take us back to our world!

00:18:49.546 --> 00:18:51.965
We have to get them back.

00:18:53.175 --> 00:18:54.676
Greg!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:18:59.348
But...

00:18:59.348 --> 00:19:03.644
It doesn't look like it will stop.
Should we wait for the next one?

00:19:03.644 --> 00:19:07.022
Are you kidding?
We gotta get on, no matter what.

00:19:07.022 --> 00:19:09.733
But how?

00:19:09.733 --> 00:19:11.485
Give me your hand.

00:19:13.237 --> 00:19:17.407
You're gonna make me touch
something creepy again, aren't you?

00:19:17.407 --> 00:19:19.535
That I won't deny.

00:19:19.535 --> 00:19:21.912
I thought so.

00:19:21.912 --> 00:19:25.082
So? What do I have to do?

00:19:25.082 --> 00:19:26.959
When I say, "Now!"

00:19:26.959 --> 00:19:32.840
grab onto whatever your hand touches
and pull like you're gonna rip it apart.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:36.718
Whatever I see, you should be able to touch.

00:19:36.718 --> 00:19:40.264
I don't know about this. It sounds dangerous.

00:19:40.264 --> 00:19:43.684
It's super dangerous,
and the timing must be near perfect.

00:19:44.768 --> 00:19:47.729
I don't know if I can do this.

00:19:48.939 --> 00:19:53.110
It'll work out... as long as we have each other.

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:54.111
You stole my--

00:19:54.111 --> 00:19:55.904
Here we go!

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:01.910
Now!

00:20:16.133 --> 00:20:18.260
We're alive.

00:20:24.016 --> 00:20:25.642
What are you doing?

00:20:25.642 --> 00:20:28.854
N-No! Don't look.

00:20:55.547 --> 00:20:59.635
It's okay. It's okay now, Sorawo.

00:21:03.388 --> 00:21:06.266
We made it back. I'm here with you.

00:21:06.266 --> 00:21:10.062
Don't worry. We have each other.

00:21:10.062 --> 00:21:12.898
Jeez, what the hell's their problem?

00:21:12.898 --> 00:21:16.068
Their calls are really weird.

00:21:18.987 --> 00:21:22.783
...the tracks to get back.
All we see is grassland and mountains.

00:21:22.783 --> 00:21:25.744
...because it's a lifeline.

00:21:25.744 --> 00:21:29.498
Error... trap. Probably safe.

00:21:29.498 --> 00:21:34.169
So many questions and answers
that I got scared and apologized.

00:21:34.169 --> 00:21:38.340
How do you know it's grandpa
if he only has one leg?

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:40.425
Speaking nonsense to oneself.

00:21:40.425 --> 00:21:42.511
This is the end.

00:21:42.511 --> 00:21:47.099
Yikes! What the hell was that?
I wish I'd never listened to it!

00:21:47.099 --> 00:21:50.602
They're gonna pay for this!

00:21:53.272 --> 00:21:55.274
So...

00:21:57.568 --> 00:21:58.068
...where... are we?

00:21:58.068 --> 00:22:01.655
"The Meat Train"
...where... are we?

00:22:01.655 --> 00:22:01.989
"The Meat Train"

00:22:11.582 --> 00:22:15.836
<i>My hair was tossed by the cold wind</i>

00:22:15.836 --> 00:22:19.965
<i>Did you notice me shut the window?</i>

00:22:19.965 --> 00:22:24.261
<i>I lose my nerve when we get so close</i>

00:22:24.261 --> 00:22:28.140
<i>I don't need something that won't last</i>

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:30.267
<i>Flashbacks hurt</i>

00:22:30.267 --> 00:22:31.894
<i>Ever-lingering shadows</i>

00:22:31.894 --> 00:22:36.064
<i>I know I'm too bound by the past, aren't I?</i>

00:22:36.064 --> 00:22:38.483
<i>Hey, this feeling we felt</i>

00:22:38.483 --> 00:22:44.072
<i>There's no doubt about it,</i>
<i>it's got to be special</i>

00:22:44.072 --> 00:22:47.910
<i>You and me, crisscrossing emotions</i>

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:52.122
<i>I don't want to look back with regret</i>

00:22:52.122 --> 00:22:56.960
<i>I tell myself to believe</i>

00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:00.923
<i>And I tell my heart,</i>
<i>trust me, trust me, so sparkly</i>

00:23:00.923 --> 00:23:04.718
<i>It's the rhythm of a racing pulse</i>

00:23:04.718 --> 00:23:08.931
<i>As I gazed at your outstretched hand</i>

00:23:08.931 --> 00:23:15.062
<i>I decided I'd put my trust in you</i>

00:23:15.062 --> 00:23:23.529
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>

00:23:23.529 --> 00:23:30.869
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will</i>

00:23:31.995 --> 00:23:32.496
"Onakiwa Pub"

00:23:32.496 --> 00:23:33.789
"Onakiwa Pub"
That was scary.

00:23:33.789 --> 00:23:36.124
"Onakiwa Pub"
We celebrated our survival
with a shopping spree.

00:23:36.124 --> 00:23:36.291
"Onakiwa Pub"
Here's to a job well done!

00:23:37.209 --> 00:23:39.169
We sure bought a lot,
but I don't remember any of it.

00:23:39.169 --> 00:23:41.505
You don't even remember?

00:23:41.505 --> 00:23:43.674
I know! I'll send Kozakura a brag text.

00:23:43.674 --> 00:23:44.967
I bet she'll love it.

00:23:44.967 --> 00:23:45.926
"We cheated death!"
I bet she'll love it.

00:23:45.926 --> 00:23:47.072
"We cheated death!"
